            <ArticleTitle>In vivo uptake of azithromycin in human coronary plaques.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>789-91, A9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Ten patients with symptomatic coronary artery disease received oral azithromycin for 3 days and underwent directional atherectomy on the third day. Azithromycin was found in all plaque samples with a median concentration of 284 ng/ml (95% confidence interval 163 to 517 ng/ml).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
